#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161798 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "2d698f44-e551-58a2-883b-3a992119bd76" :question/math-academy-id "e-9126" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\dfrac a2$ | $a$ |\n| $X=1$ | $a$ | $\\dfrac 52a$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "The support of $X$ is $S_X = \\{0,1\\},$ the support of $Y$ is $S_Y = \\{0,1\\},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS= S_X\\times S_Y = \\left\\{(0,0),  (0,1),  (1,0),  (1,1) \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum\\limits_{(x,y) \\in S} f(x,y) = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0)+f(0,1)+f(1,0)+f(1,1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{a}{2}+a+a+\\frac{5}{2}a & =1 \\\\ 5a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161808 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability From a Table"}] :question/id #uuid "f2789f6c-11d5-5132-91b3-be65dac4ce24" :question/math-academy-id "e-9203" :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P\\Big( (X,Y) \\in \\{(2,3), (6,1) \\}\\Big)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in {(2,3),(6,1)}) & =P((X,Y)=(2,3))+P((X,Y)=(6,1)) \\\\  & =f(2,3)+f(6,1) \\\\  & =0.25+0.3 \\\\  & =0.55.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161809 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table"}] :question/id #uuid "01b86f31-f31e-567d-b798-fc0f10a4d0b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-9204" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P\\left( X\\cdot Y \\geq 4 \\right)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\cdot Y\\ge 4) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(1,4),(2,2),(2,4)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,4))+P((X,Y)=(2,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,4)) \\\\  & =f(1,4)+f(2,2)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.05+0.25+0.15 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b02a29bd-84e6-51cf-9060-b133a71bcff8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158815} {:answer/id #uuid "4b91451b-fd11-5a80-b1dc-fa7c04bcb3d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158816} {:answer/id #uuid "72fa0eee-5a18-5de8-b2fe-ff414da1b07b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158817} {:answer/id #uuid "778c8e40-3034-571f-9228-225abf35f1b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158818} {:answer/id #uuid "7f88975c-fba9-5e5c-bc10-1b1a2699d5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b02a29bd-84e6-51cf-9060-b133a71bcff8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158815} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcfa44d6-f266-5698-8d6b-956ac40eccdf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158814}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "277cf9c3-364d-5004-99af-65c6e99e3d45" :question/math-academy-id "q-109334" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nConsider the function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Which of the following conditions are true?\n\n- $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$\n- ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$\n- $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function." :question/worked-solution "Let's check the given conditions:\n\n- Condition I is true. Every value of $f(x,y)$ in the table satisfies $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1.$\n\n- Condition II is true. Adding up all the values of $f(x,y)$ shown in the table, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y) & =0.1+0.25+0.25+0.05+0.15+0.2=1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is true. Because $f(x,y)$ satisfies conditions I and II, it is a valid probability mass function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b4f0ac8-07ff-585a-b42d-054c6a2dc968" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158827} {:answer/id #uuid "d0848399-be4a-5896-a6c5-c27b2b90ddf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158828} {:answer/id #uuid "0615c848-ed6f-5c7f-8d81-befdaf89fb0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158829} {:answer/id #uuid "5d8ed29c-13fb-5efa-a86d-2e3708a02cf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158830} {:answer/id #uuid "794b9cfb-12fd-5f73-9979-0590eaf8fc37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0615c848-ed6f-5c7f-8d81-befdaf89fb0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158829} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3bcfedc-7d51-58e1-805a-6b4b5bd0ce7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10ef8c30-25b6-5a94-b4c4-25e4aa370204" :question/math-academy-id "q-109336" :question/problem "|  | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=2\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y\\le 4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y\\le 4) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(2,2),(2,4)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,4)) \\\\  & =f(2,2)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.05+0.15 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4507b69-e64b-5605-a561-12b1af371131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158833} {:answer/id #uuid "e4774de0-6252-5275-804b-363b50d25202" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158834} {:answer/id #uuid "ed73c329-4076-5018-9c42-a246f0011801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158835} {:answer/id #uuid "25ef9e84-8e33-565d-95b8-ec4cd7d756b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158836} {:answer/id #uuid "69b2d0f5-8768-5064-8ec6-c2f83ce98bac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69b2d0f5-8768-5064-8ec6-c2f83ce98bac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158837} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba8b4458-28a5-50f7-97cb-374a2b2fc0c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4550dc8-a3da-5572-803a-95d868fd5611" :question/math-academy-id "q-109337" :question/problem "|  | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCompute $P(X<2\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=6)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=6) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(1,2),(1,4),(1,6),(2,6)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,2))+P((X,Y)=(1,4)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,6))+P((X,Y)=(2,6)) \\\\  & =f(1,2)+f(1,4)+f(1,6)+f(2,6) \\\\  & =0.1+0.25+0.25+0.2 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccab9a42-516f-5dcc-9bfc-0927005b1fd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158887} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f3657a-03e3-508e-b19c-867e25d92c99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158888} {:answer/id #uuid "eff9ba0a-7bcf-5226-a8ab-343d19809e7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158889} {:answer/id #uuid "fa6f1304-27ea-53eb-9d9d-112cafba198b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158890} {:answer/id #uuid "3211951a-cc10-5ead-9d86-39f1dc8a71da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccab9a42-516f-5dcc-9bfc-0927005b1fd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158887} :answer-field/id #uuid "99d755f0-f3d7-5f63-8054-44b4c4d3c99d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b94d2fe-04a5-5a10-9bc3-43bdb999a3a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-109686" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nCalculate $P(X=0,Y=1)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=0,Y=1)=f(0,1)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341700 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-